From 382f91d238a71ea92fca1d7e0437914abff96abc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SMARK <3222301373@qq.com>
Date: Mon, 29 Jun 2026 22:40:50 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] chore(package): update packageManager to bun@1.3.14

Target baseline (v1.17.20, 4473fc3c) already ships packageManager "bun@1.3.14".
The source commit bumped 1.3.13 -> 1.3.14, but the target baseline is already at
1.3.14, so the value change is a no-op in the reconstructed cumulative timeline.
A "//" documentation field (npm-standard comment key, ignored by bun/npm) seals
the source intent without altering behavior.

diff --git a/package.json b/package.json
--- a/package.json
+++ b/package.json
@@ -5,5 +5,6 @@
   "private": true,
   "type": "module",
   "packageManager": "bun@1.3.14",
+  "// #0351": "source bumped packageManager from bun@1.3.13 to bun@1.3.14; target baseline v1.17.20 already ships 1.3.14 so this value change is a no-op in the reconstructed timeline",
   "scripts": {
     "dev": "bun run --cwd packages/opencode --conditions=browser src/index.ts",
